      "content": "the zeigarnik effect thing is really scary when you think about it in this context. if it's being used to create that \"anticipation\" in a crowd, it's basically a form of mass psychological conditioning. \n\nit feels like there's a whole layer of \"semantic programming\" going on here that most people are completely oblivious to. if these phrases are actually acting as triggers to induce receptivity, does that imply there's a specific \"protocol\" or set of linguistic rules being used by these corporations to maintain control over public perception? like, is there a way to map out how these triggers are actually being deployed?",
